        {
          "title": "Digitize Your Handwriting",
          "subtitle": "Feb 2016 - May 2016",
          "subComponenets": [
            {
              "description": [
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "Associated with Rochester Institute of Technology"
                },
                {
                  "type": "textComponent",
                  "text": "The objective of this project is to convert handwritten text in an image into a digital format in the form of a document. For this purpose, Optical Character Recognition (OCR) is developed to meet our demands. A training set containing alphabets of the English language is used as a basis for comparison with the texts in the image. Based on this comparison, the English alphabet that closely resembles the handwritten text is chosen as the alphabet that it is most likely to be, and is written into the digital document. An ideal model would be able to represent all the text in the image in a digitized format correctly. This model performed quite well for my set of images used for training the model."
                }
              ]
            }
